    "catalog:format": "2",
    "catalog:tags": "basin, wash basin, pedestal, bathroom",
    "catalog:note": "Pedestal wash basin against the wall. rim 0.85. A D-shaped rim slab 0.04 thick, two outline sweeps of true arcs with a round bowl of radius 0.15 through them; under it a revolved bowl whose outline has its wall, curved in 6 chords per arc, and a flat floor 0.13 below the rim with a metal waste in its centre hole, on a tapered round pedestal. The waste port is at the foot of the pedestal: the trap is inside it, not drawn. Parts under radius 0.04 build as polygonal prisms at true size.",
    "catalog:basedOn": "Drafting standard key dimensions (practice, Neufert / Metric Handbook), unverified: wash basin 0.55 x 0.45, rim 0.85; EN 14688 not read. Bowl depth 0.13, the D and the pedestal taper are the author's, unverified. Port sizes from the drafting standard (BS EN 12056-2), unverified",
